Hexagon HTP: the fused state step and the HVX conv step of a gated delta net layer at one token

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches of patches/series before this one.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp          the graph match and the switch
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-gdn-match.h           the chain checks, with a reason for each failure
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-ops.h             two opcodes
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-ctx.h             two prototypes
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/main.c                the dispatch
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/CMakeLists.txt        the new kernel file
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gated-delta-net-ops.c the state step (the plain kernel with other pointers)
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c        the conv step (new file)
    tests/test-backend-ops.cpp                      GDN_CONV_STATE_FUSION and GDN_STATE_FUSION

The DSP library and the host library both change.

Switch: GGML_HEXAGON_OPFUSION_STATE=0 keeps the unfused path, 1 forces the fusion. When the
variable is not set, the fusion follows GGML_HEXAGON_OPFUSION (1 = all, or the bit 64 of the
mask). GGML_HEXAGON_OPFUSION=0 disables it with the other fusions.

What the patch does

At one token, a gated delta net layer reads its two recurrent states with GET_ROWS, updates
them, and writes them back with CPY. The host matches two chains once per graph and emits one
op for each:

    GET_ROWS(cache_r, s_copy) -> CONCAT(., x^T) -> SSM_CONV -> SILU, CPY(view, slot of cache_r)
        -> HTP_OP_GDN_CONV_STEP
    GET_ROWS(cache_s, s_copy) -> GATED_DELTA_NET(K = 1), CPY(state tail, slot of cache_s)
        -> HTP_OP_GDN_STATE_STEP

The DSP reads the source slot index from s_copy and writes the destination slot of the CPY.
When the two slots are the same, the update is in place. The match needs one token, one
sequence, one CPY, no other reader of the replaced tensors, and no other node that touches
the cache inside the chain span. Every other case keeps the unfused path. The state_zero
SCALE of build_rs comes before the chain, thus it stays a separate op and runs first.

Numerics

The state step runs the single-token thread of the plain GATED_DELTA_NET kernel. Only the
three base pointers differ (state in, state out, attention out). The result is the same as
the unfused DSP path bit for bit. The conv step adds the d_conv products in F32 in the order
of the CPU reference, and applies the SiLU with the two HVX routines of the SILU op.

The conv step on the vector unit

A scalar loop on data in VTCM costs about 350 us for each GDN_CONV_STEP op. Scalar loads
and stores to VTCM are slow, and no other kernel of this backend does that. The conv kernel
here is HVX only: it reads DDR with unaligned vector loads, it keeps a block of 32 channels
in registers, and it writes DDR with unaligned vector stores. The layout change from 3 lanes
for each channel (the slot) to 4 lanes for each channel (the taps) uses rotates and masks,
four vdeal ops split the block into tap planes, and the four products go together in the
order of the CPU reference. The SiLU is the sigmoid and the multiply of the SILU op. The new
slot lanes come back from the 4-lane block with rotates and masks. Only d_conv = 4 is fused,
and another width keeps the unfused path.

The reader check of the state output

The check "no reader of the state part of the output outside the chain" judges a view node by
its own range, and a compute node by the view that it reads. A check of the source of each
reader is not sufficient: a view node has the whole output as its source, thus the attention
view of the output fails such a check and the state fusion never matches on the real graph.
A host probe that runs the checks of htp-gdn-match.h on the one-token graph of Qwen3.5-2B
matches 18 of 18 state chains and 18 of 18 conv chains.

With GGML_HEXAGON_VERBOSE=1 the host logs one line for each candidate chain that does not
match, with the failed condition, for example:
    ggml-hex: HTP0 GDN_STATE_STEP candidate node_46 (node 46): the state part of the output has a reader outside the chain

